    "result_text": "The full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the per-city owner cap (reject creation, respond **409** when the owner's city already holds 50+ owners), mirroring the repo's existing rule pattern to keep structural impact low.\n\n**Changes:**\n1. **New `CityAtCapacityException`** (`rest/advice/`) \u2014 a small, cohesive class modeled on `DuplicateHouseholdException`: a static `rejectIfAtCapacity(city, existingOwners)` guard that counts owners with the same normalized city (case/whitespace-insensitive) and throws when the count reaches 50.\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 one added line calling the guard, alongside the existing duplicate-telephone/household checks. `addOwner` stays CC 1.\n3. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 one new small handler mapping the exception to `409 CONFLICT`, identical in shape to the two existing conflict handlers.\n\nEach function I touched or added stays trivial (CC 1), and the new behaviour lives in its own low-complexity class rather than growing any existing method. The new acceptance test `coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` and the full suite pass.",
